      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for these. they're a good start but a bit surface-level for a high school policy round. my students need to move past the basic talking points. can you go deeper into the philosophical side of the sovereignty argument? like, help them frame it not just as \"patrol the border,\" but as a fundamental necessity for the existence of a social contract? i want them to have arguments that feel intellectually unassailable.",
